Java libraries (lib/ in the release)
------------------------------------
Most of the roughly 180 jars are Apache-2.0 (Play, Pekko, Netty, Jackson, Guava, Caffeine,
Tapir, ScalikeJDBC, Flyway, Nimbus, play-mailer, scala-csv, scalawiki and others), MIT,
or BSD (TwelveMonkeys ImageIO, ASM, ...). Apache-2.0 code is combined into this
GPL-3.0-or-later work as GPL-3.0 allows. The ones with other terms:

- jaxb-impl 2.2.5 and jaxb-api 2.3.1 (through scalawiki-wlx and Sweble): offered under
  CDDL-1.1 or GPL-2.0 with the Classpath Exception. Option chosen: GPL-2.0 with the
  Classpath Exception (text below and licenses/GPL-2.0.txt). The jars are unmodified
  and used as separate libraries; the exception allows linking them with modules under
  other licences.
- rats-runtime (xtc) 1.15.0 (through Sweble): LGPL-2.1. Unmodified, dynamically linked;
  text in licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt.
- logback-classic and logback-core 1.6.4: EPL-2.0 or LGPL-2.1. Option chosen: LGPL-2.1
  (licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt).
- mariadb-java-client 3.5.3: LGPL-2.1-or-later (licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt).
- jakarta.mail 1.6.7: EPL-2.0, GPL-2.0 with Classpath Exception or EDL-1.0 (BSD-3-Clause).
  Option chosen: EDL-1.0. jakarta.activation 1.2.1: EDL-1.0.
- MIT: chronoscala, ficus, odelay, scallop, progressbar, sysout-over-slf4j, checker-qual,
  enumeratum, jsoup, slf4j (api and jul-to-slf4j), cats (core and kernel), jawn-parser.
- Apache-2.0: retry, scala-csv, jsr305, jcip-annotations (stephenc repackaging).
- BSD-3-Clause: paranamer, jline, TwelveMonkeys ImageIO, ASM.
- aopalliance 1.0: public domain. reactive-streams 1.0.4: MIT-0.
- scalawiki (core, wlx, http-extensions): Apache-2.0, by the same maintainer.
- tyrex 1.0.1 (Exolab licence, with a credit clause) is not bundled: it is excluded
  in build.sbt because nothing uses it.

